Homework 1 is a node spring system calculator

To evaluate the system, call/run Homework1.py

Using nodes.txt, input coordinates to establish nodes on individual lines.
Then, connect the nodes in springs.txt. A spring is identified by the indexes of two nodes, and the stiffness.
The form is as follows with one spring per line: indx1, indx2, stiffness
Identify which of the nodes are to be free in free_nodes.txt. each free node should be separated by commas.

To change to the explicit integrator rather than the implicit integrator, uncomment out line 159, and comment out 160.

Or, replace myInt with myIntExp, as below.
  #x_new, u_new = myIntExp(t_new, x_old, u_old, free_DOF, stiffness_matrix, index_matrix, m, dt, l_k) # I added l_k to this function
